<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xian of Han</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">181–234</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Liu Xie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xian of Han, Liu Xie, was the last emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a>, reigning from 189 to 220. A puppet of successive warlords, he came under the control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-cao">Cao Cao</a> in 196, who ruled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in his name. In 220 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-pi">Cao Pi</a> forced him to abdicate and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Wei dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-xian-of-han.jpg" alt="Emperor Xian of Han" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Xian_Qing_illustration.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
